╭─ Issue description ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Issue Title: [BUG] Heuristic count_tokens returns 0 for toolResult content with json blocks                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Description:                                                                                                                                    │
│ # Overview                                                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The heuristic `count_tokens` estimator silently returns 0 for tool results that use `json` content blocks. This breaks the `ContextOffloader`   │
│ plugin's threshold check whenever native token counting is unavailable (e.g., `bedrock:CountTokens` IAM denied, model not on the CountTokens    │
│ allowlist, network failure → fallback path).                                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ **Root cause:** `_count_content_block_tokens` in `strands-py/src/strands/models/model.py` only counts `text` items inside `toolResult` content. │
│ The `json` branch is missing, even though `count_json` is already passed into the function and used elsewhere (e.g., `toolUse.input`).          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Implementation Requirements                                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Technical Approach                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ **File to modify:** `strands-py/src/strands/models/model.py`                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ In `_count_content_block_tokens` (lines 60-64), the `toolResult` branch currently only handles `text` items:                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ if "toolResult" in block:                                                                                                                       │
│     tool_result = block["toolResult"]                                                                                                           │
│     for item in tool_result.get("content", []):                                                                                                 │
│         if "text" in item:                                                                                                                      │
│             total += count_text(item["text"])                                                                                                   │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Add the missing `json` handling to mirror how `toolUse.input` is counted:                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ if "toolResult" in block:                                                                                                                       │
│     tool_result = block["toolResult"]                                                                                                           │
│     for item in tool_result.get("content", []):                                                                                                 │
│         if "text" in item:                                                                                                                      │
│             total += count_text(item["text"])                                                                                                   │
│         if "json" in item:                                                                                                                      │
│             total += count_json(item["json"])                                                                                                   │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The `count_json` callable is already a parameter of the function and uses `json.dumps(obj) / 2` for heuristic estimation (consistent with the   │
│ function's own docstring).                                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Files to Modify                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ | File | Change |                                                                                                                               │
│ |------|--------|                                                                                                                               │
│ | `strands-py/src/strands/models/model.py` | Add `json` branch in `toolResult` loop inside `_count_content_block_tokens` |                      │
│ | `strands-py/tests/strands/models/test_model.py` | Add regression test(s) for `toolResult` with `json` content |                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Acceptance Criteria                                                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ - [ ] `_count_content_block_tokens` counts tokens for `json` items in `toolResult` content using the `count_json` callable                      │
│ - [ ] `_estimate_tokens_with_heuristic` returns a non-zero value for messages containing `toolResult` with `json` content blocks                │
│ - [ ] The fix uses the same heuristic pattern as `toolUse.input` (i.e., `json.dumps(obj) / 2`)                                                  │
│ - [ ] A regression test verifies that `count_tokens` returns the expected non-zero value for a `toolResult` containing `json` content           │
│ - [ ] A regression test verifies mixed `text` + `json` content in a single `toolResult`                                                         │
│ - [ ] Existing tests continue to pass (no regressions)                                                                                          │
│ - [ ] Code passes `hatch fmt --formatter` and `hatch fmt --linter`                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Reproduction Test Case                                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ from strands.models.model import _estimate_tokens_with_heuristic                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ messages = [{                                                                                                                                   │
│     "role": "user",                                                                                                                             │
│     "content": [{                                                                                                                               │
│         "toolResult": {                                                                                                                         │
│             "status": "success",                                                                                                                │
│             "content": [{"json": {"x": "lorem ipsum " * 1000}}],                                                                                │
│         }                                                                                                                                       │
│     }]                                                                                                                                          │
│ }]                                                                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ tokens = _estimate_tokens_with_heuristic(messages)                                                                                              │
│ # Before fix: 0                                                                                                                                 │
│ # After fix: ~6001 (ceil(len(json.dumps({"x": "lorem ipsum " * 1000})) / 2))                                                                    │
│ assert tokens > 0                                                                                                                               │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Downstream Impact                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The `ContextOffloader` plugin (`strands-py/src/strands/vended_plugins/context_offloader/plugin.py`) relies on `model.count_tokens` to determine │
│ when to offload large tool results. When `count_tokens` returns 0 for `json` content, the offloader's threshold check (`token_count <=          │
│ self._max_result_tokens`) always passes and offloading never triggers — silently making the plugin a no-op for JSON tool results.               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Notes                                                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ - This is a 2-line production code change with regression tests                                                                                 │
│ - No workflow changes needed                                                                                                                    │
│ - No breaking changes — this only adds previously-missing functionality                                                                         │
│ - The `ToolResultContent` TypedDict already defines `json: Any` as a valid content type                                                         │
│ - For future maintainability: consider adding a code comment noting which `ToolResultContent` fields are handled vs. skipped (e.g., `image` and │
│ `document` are binary and intentionally not counted by the heuristic)                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ---                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ *Original report by @sonerkuyar*                                                                                                                │
